      "id": 1,
      "text": "Silver Lake Colony was established in 2011 as a daughter colony divided from the Hillcrest Hutterite Colony near Garden City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/silver_lake_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Silver Lake Colony is a member of the Hutterian Brethren and specifically affiliates with the Schmiedeleut Group 2.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/silver_lake_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community at Silver Lake Colony follows Anabaptist principles emphasizing communal living, pacifism, and separation from worldly powers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/silver_lake_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fertile agricultural land in Clark County was chosen for Silver Lake Colony to support its farming-based economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/silver_lake_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Silver Lake Colony operates as a tax-exempt religious organization under the Internal Revenue Code for apostolic associations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/silver_lake_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Flat and gently rolling prairie terrain makes Silver Lake Colony ideal for mechanized agriculture and crop cultivation.",
